# One customer per line:
#   Drive folder name[|aha_org_id[,aha_org_id2,...]][|Display Name][|pdf_folder_id]
#
# Field 1 -- Drive folder name (required)
#   The EXACT name of the customer's own folder, which sits at
#   <region>/<customer> in the Customers shared drive. Lookup is exact-match,
#   not fuzzy, and rejects a same-named folder nested any deeper (see
#   find_customer_folder in scripts/drive-lib.sh). This is the DRIVE folder
#   name, which is not always the customer's real name -- Sony's folder is
#   "Sony Interactive", not "Sony Interactive Entertainment". It's also the
#   Aha! search term when field 2 is empty.
#
# Field 2 -- Aha idea-organization id(s) (optional)
#   Pins the Aha! organization explicitly instead of searching by name. Use it
#   whenever the Drive folder name and the right Aha org diverge, or a plain
#   search would be too broad/ambiguous (e.g. "X Corporation" fuzzy-matches
#   dozens of unrelated "*Corporation" orgs in Aha with no exact-match guard
#   by default). Comma-separate for a customer with more than one legitimate
#   Aha org.
#
# Field 3 -- Display name (optional, defaults to field 1)
#   What the customer-facing PDF and the Sheet title actually say -- set it
#   when the Drive folder name would be wrong to put in front of a customer.
#   It overrides field 1 for the Sheet title and the PDF heading/filename;
#   field 1 still drives folder lookup. Changing it renames the Sheet the
#   pipeline looks for, so rename any existing Sheet to match or a second one
#   gets created next to it.
#
# Field 4 -- pdf-reports destination folder id (optional)
#   Pins the customer-facing bundle to an explicit My Drive location (forwarded
#   as --pdf-folder). The id is the customer's Customer/<Name>/FRs/pdf-reports
#   folder in My Drive, which must already exist. From it the pipeline derives,
#   without any extra ids:
#     - the parent FRs folder, which receives a customer-facing Sheet copy, and
#     - a sibling csv-exports folder (created if missing), which receives the CSV.
#   The customer-facing PDF goes into the pinned pdf-reports folder itself. The
#   internal Sheet still lands in its original shared-drive <Customer>/CS/FRs
#   folder, so that long-standing link is unaffected. To set this while leaving
#   the display name (field 3) empty, use two pipes: name|org||folderid.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. run-all.sh processes
# every customer here on each scheduled run.

# This file is the documented example, not the live list.
#
# The real list names customers, their Aha! organization ids and their Drive
# folder ids. This repository is public, and anything committed here is also
# copied into /nix/store, which is world-readable on the host. So the live list
# is kept off both: it lives at apps.cli.aha-fr-report.customersFile, which
# defaults to ~/.config/aha-fr-report/customers.txt, alongside the rendered
# secrets rather than inside the flake.
#
# To set it up on a host:
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/aha-fr-report
#   cp <this file> ~/.config/aha-fr-report/customers.txt
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/aha-fr-report/customers.txt
#
# The two example rows below are inert. Replace them.

Example Customer
Second Example|1234567890123456789|Second Example Inc.
